		{
			dependencies: ["44EA00000000000E"]
			description: [
				"&2&lFirst Machines.&r"
				""
				"Water gave you torque; now torque buys you &lelectricity&r. An Industrial Keystone, your first Mekanism machines, and grid power that never sleeps."
				""
				"&cThe gate you already passed:&r the Metallurgic Infuser is built around your Precision Mechanism. The next gate: &cAE2's Inscriber demands an Advanced Control Circuit&r - the digital age waits for the electric one."
			]
			icon: "skyforge:industrial_keystone"
			id: "2102000000000001"
			rewards: [{
				id: "2102000000000101"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 40
			}]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.5d
			subtitle: "&7Sky metal becomes industry"
			tasks: [{
				id: "2102000000000201"
				title: "Enter the Machine Age"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "&2First Machines"
			x: -12.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["2102000000000001"]
			description: [
				"The &eIndustrial Keystone&r is the master key to tech. Craft it from Sky Steel, redstone and a diamond."
				""
				"In a crafting grid it bridges Sky Dust into &7Osmium&r, &7Certus Quartz&r and &7Uraninite&r, and Sky Steel into &7Mekanism Steel&r - the ores the void refuses to give you."
			]
			icon: "skyforge:industrial_keystone"
			id: "2102000000000002"
			rewards: [{
				count: 2
				id: "2102000000000102"
				item: "skyforge:industrial_keystone"
				type: "item"
			}]
			shape: "diamond"
			size: 1.25d
			subtitle: "&7The master key to tech"
			tasks: [{
				id: "2102000000000202"
				item: "skyforge:industrial_keystone"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&2The Industrial Keystone"
			x: -10.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["2102000000000002"]
			description: [
				"Bridge Sky Steel into &eMekanism Steel&r, then press it into a &eSteel Casing&r - the shell of nearly every Mekanism machine you are about to build."
				""
				"&e&lSteel Casings are the tax on everything.&r Enrichment Chamber, Crusher, Smelter, Purification, Injection, the Digital Miner, the Teleporter - every one of them is a casing plus contents. You will not build four. You will build forty."
				""
				"&e&lSo automate it early.&r The chain is &7iron + coal dust &8→&7 steel dust &8→&7 smelt &8→&7 steel ingot&r, then casings. Mekanism's own machines can run that whole line, which means the first thing you should build with Mekanism is more Mekanism."
				""
				"&7SkyForge gives you a keystone bridge to Mekanism Steel directly. Use it to get the first few casings, then switch to the real chain once your Enrichment Chamber is live - the bridge does not scale.&r"
				""
				"&8Stockpile steel. Every time you think you have enough, you are about three machines short."
			]
			icon: "mekanism:ingot_steel"
			id: "2102000000000003"
			rewards: [{
				count: 2
				id: "2102000000000103"
				item: "mekanism:steel_casing"
				type: "item"
			}]
			subtitle: "&7The metal machines are made of"
			tasks: [{
				count: 4L
				id: "2102000000000203"
				item: "mekanism:ingot_steel"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&2Real Steel"
			x: -8.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["2102000000000003"]
			description: [
				"The &eMetallurgic Infuser&r is Mekanism's gateway machine - it infuses materials with redstone, carbon, tin and more to make enriched alloys and steel."
				""
				"&cIts recipe is built around your Precision Mechanism&r - kinetics literally inside the machine. &9Build it and the full Mekanism branch opens in Act II.&r Osmium comes from the keystone bridge, or from sieving gravel with an iron mesh."
			]
			icon: "mekanism:metallurgic_infuser"
			id: "2102000000000004"
			rewards: [{
				count: 4
				id: "2102000000000104"
				item: "mekanism:enriched_redstone"
				type: "item"
			}]
			shape: "gear"
			subtitle: "&7Opens the Mekanism branch"
			tasks: [{
				id: "2102000000000204"
				item: "mekanism:metallurgic_infuser"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Metallurgy 101"
			x: -6.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["2102000000000004"]
			description: [
				"Infuse redstone into &eEnriched Redstone&r - the concentrated form Mekanism uses in circuits, energy tablets and control components. Make a stack; you will need it constantly."
				""
				"&e&lHow the Metallurgic Infuser works.&r It has two inputs: the &litem&r you are upgrading, and an &linfusion type&r loaded from a second slot. Put redstone dust in the infusion slot and it fills an internal buffer - that buffer is then spent on whatever passes through."
				""
				"&7Infusion types you will use constantly:&r"
				"&7- &fRedstone&7 - enriched redstone, enriched alloy"
				"&7- &fDiamond&7 - reinforced alloy"
				"&7- &fCarbon&7 (coal/charcoal) - steel dust"
				"&7- &fRefined Obsidian&7 - atomic alloy"
				""
				"&8Load the infusion buffer well ahead of what you are making - a half-empty buffer silently stalls the machine mid-batch and it looks like it has jammed."
				""
				"&c&lRemember the Infuser itself was gated&r - it needs a Create Precision Mechanism. That was deliberate: kinetics buy electricity, and this block is the receipt."
			]
			icon: "mekanism:enriched_redstone"
			id: "2102000000000005"
			rewards: [{
				id: "2102000000000105"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Concentrated redstone"
			tasks: [{
				count: 4L
				id: "2102000000000205"
				item: "mekanism:enriched_redstone"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Enriched Materials"
			x: -6.0d
			y: -1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["2102000000000005"]
			description: [
				"A &eHeat Generator&r burns lava, coal or fuel to make your first Forge Energy. Wire it into the Sky Assembler with Universal Cables and the ingots roll in without you."
				""
				"This is the beginning of the end of doing anything by hand."
			]
			icon: "mekanismgenerators:heat_generator"
			id: "2102000000000006"
			rewards: [{
				count: 8
				id: "2102000000000106"
				item: "minecraft:coal_block"
				type: "item"
			}]
			shape: "gear"
			subtitle: "&7Your first grid power"
			tasks: [{
				id: "2102000000000206"
				item: "mekanismgenerators:heat_generator"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Power On"
			x: -4.0d
			y: -1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["2102000000000006"]
			description: [
				"The &eEnergized Smelter&r smelts with power instead of fuel, faster and cleaner than any furnace. Route it into your ore-chunk pipeline and forget about coal."
				""
				"&e&lThis is where you stop feeding furnaces by hand.&r No fuel slot, no ash, no refilling - it draws FE and runs as long as the grid holds. Everything a furnace can smelt, it smelts faster."
				""
				"&e&lUpgrades slot into every Mekanism machine&r, and this is a good place to learn them:"
				"&7- &fSpeed Upgrade&7 - faster processing, higher power draw."
				"&7- &fEnergy Upgrade&7 - bigger internal buffer, less sensitive to grid dips."
				"&7- &fMuffling Upgrade&7 - silences it. Put these in everything or your base will be unbearable."
				""
				"&7Right-click the machine, open the upgrade slot on the left, and drop them in. Up to 8 of each.&r"
				""
				"&e&lWire it into the ore line:&r Crusher or Enrichment Chamber output &8→&7 Energized Smelter &8→&7 ingot chest&r. That is your sieve chain finally running end to end without you."
			]
			icon: "mekanism:energized_smelter"
			id: "2102000000000007"
			rewards: [{
				id: "2102000000000107"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Smelt with electricity"
			tasks: [{
				id: "2102000000000207"
				item: "mekanism:energized_smelter"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Energized Smelter"
			x: -2.0d
			y: -1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["2102000000000004"]
			description: [
				"The &eEnrichment Chamber&r is your first ore multiplier: one ingot's worth of chunk in, two dusts out. Smelt the dust and you have doubled every metal you sieve."
				""
				"This is where the void stops being stingy."
			]
			icon: "mekanism:enrichment_chamber"
			id: "2102000000000008"
			rewards: [{
				count: 8
				id: "2102000000000108"
				item: "minecraft:iron_ingot"
				type: "item"
			}]
			shape: "gear"
			subtitle: "&7Double your ore"
			tasks: [{
				id: "2102000000000208"
				item: "mekanism:enrichment_chamber"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9The Enrichment Chamber"
			x: -4.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["2102000000000006"]
			description: [
				"A &eCrusher&r grinds ingots back into dust and clears the way to Mekanism's deeper ore chains. Cheap, fast, and a prerequisite for the good stuff."
				""
				"&e&lThe Crusher is half of your first doubling.&r On its own it turns ingots back into dust - which sounds pointless until you realise the pairing:"
				""
				"&7Ore chunk &8→&7 &fEnrichment Chamber&7 &8→&7 2x dust &8→&7 &fEnergized Smelter&7 &8→&7 2 ingots&r"
				""
				"&e&lThat is 2x ore, and it is the entry rung of a ladder that goes to 5x:&r"
				"&7- &a2x&7 Enrichment Chamber"
				"&7- &a3x&7 + Purification Chamber (needs oxygen)"
				"&7- &a4x&7 + Chemical Injection Chamber (needs hydrogen chloride)"
				"&7- &a5x&7 + Chemical Dissolution + Washer + Crystallizer"
				""
				"Each tier adds machines &lin front&r of the previous one rather than replacing it, so nothing you build here is wasted later."
				""
				"&7The Crusher also makes coal dust for steel, bio fuel from plants, and is the cheapest way to turn surplus tools and armour back into usable metal.&r"
			]
			icon: "mekanism:crusher"
			id: "2102000000000009"
			rewards: [{
				id: "2102000000000109"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Grind it down"
			tasks: [{
				id: "2102000000000209"
				item: "mekanism:crusher"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9The Crusher"
			x: -4.0d
			y: -3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["2102000000000008"]
			description: [
				"The &eOsmium Compressor&r combines osmium with materials to make Mekanism's control circuits and refined alloys. Feed it osmium from the keystone or the sieve."
				""
				"&e&lIt runs on liquid osmium, not ingots.&r The compressor takes a &lgas&r input - molten osmium - produced by feeding osmium ingots or dust into it, plus the item you want to compress. If it looks stuck, check the gas buffer before anything else."
				""
				"&e&lWhat comes out of it:&r"
				"&7- &fBasic Control Circuits&7 - the component you will make thousands of"
				"&7- &fRefined Obsidian / Refined Glowstone Ingots&7 - the late-tier alloys"
				""
				"&7Osmium is the single most-consumed metal in Mekanism, and it does not drop below an iron mesh. If this machine keeps running dry, the fix is upstream - more sieves on iron or diamond mesh, not a bigger compressor.&r"
				""
				"&8Pair it with the Metallurgic Infuser and the Enrichment Chamber and you have the three blocks that produce every Mekanism intermediate. Everything else is those three, scaled."
			]
			icon: "mekanism:osmium_compressor"
			id: "210200000000000A"
			rewards: [{
				id: "210200000000010A"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Compress osmium"
			tasks: [{
				id: "210200000000020A"
				item: "mekanism:osmium_compressor"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Osmium Compressor"
			x: -2.0d
			y: -3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["267D2B1D2D8750CC"]
			description: [
				"&bThe digital age begins&r - but only now. Charge your sieved &eCertus Quartz&r and combine it into &eFluix Crystals&r - the semiconductor at the heart of every AE2 device."
				""
				"AE2 is deliberately &lmid-game&r in this pack: its Inscriber demands the Advanced Control Circuits you just learned to make. If the void was stingy with certus, the keystone bridge makes more."
			]
			icon: "ae2:fluix_crystal"
			id: "210200000000000B"
			rewards: [{
				count: 8
